  "title": "Federal Technology and Monetary Infrastructure Delta — September 17–20, 2026",
  "question": "What materially changed after the September 16 whole-government cursor across the federal technology and monetary-control stack, including changes not labeled crypto, tokenization or stablecoin?",
  "bluf": "The September 17–20 record shows broad institutional refactoring rather than one crypto event. SEC data/AI organization, machine-readable disclosure requirements, market-data incentives, outside software distribution, 23x5 resilience, Fed rate and supervisory decision paths, DTCC interfaces and government-wide procurement rules are moving on separate clocks. More activity can pass through standardized data and private software, while authoritative records, accounts, custody, clearing, correction, escalation and remedy remain assigned to named institutions. The convergence is real; a single master plan, common platform or wholesale transfer of public authority is not established.",
